67935,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.20084,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"FedEx Freight Holding Company, Inc. provides less-than-truckload freight transportation services in the United States and internationally. The company offers FedEx Freight Priority services, including next-business-day service for shipments traveling up to 600 miles and second-business-day service for shipments traveling up to 1,600 miles and backed by a money-back service guarantee if published delivery commitments are not met; and FedEx Freight Economy. It also provides surface expedite and white glove services; and LTL Select, a cloud-based transportation management system. In addition, the company offers volume and custom critical services, FedEx Freight Direct, and Retail Flex. It provides its services under the FedEx and FedEx Freight names. The company was incorporated in 2025 and is headquartered in Memphis, Tennessee.","ceo_bio":"Mr. John Alan Smith | President, CEO & Director | Age 63 | Compensation: $5.7M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 40K people. Revenue per employee of $220K ranks in the bottom quartile among Industrials peers. Stock-based compensation of $325 per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 26\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity).","financial_summary":["FedEx Freight Holding Company,  is a large-cap industrials business with a $18.5B market cap on $8.8B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 10% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The company is burning through $212M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 4.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and interest coverage runs at 9.5\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 20% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 87% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.8720121028744328},{"text":"Accruals running hot at +7.1% of assets \u2014 earnings quality bears watching","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Industrials peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Industrials sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 8% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Industrials ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Industrials tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"75,618 FedEx Freight Hldg Co $FDXF Shares Sold by Sentry LLC","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/75618-fedex-freight-hldg-co-fdxf-shares-sold-by-sentry-llc.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793876508.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.878,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"FedEx Freight (FDXF) Stock May Be 17% Undervalued Despit